In the afternoon, I ride my bicycle back to the city center.
I park it in front of the boutique.
Then I go directly to customer service.
A shop assistant stands behind the counter.
She smiles nicely.
"Hello, how can I help you?" she asks.
"Hello," I answer.
I take the yellow T-shirt out of my backpack.
"I bought this shirt today," I say.
"But unfortunately it is too small for me."
"It is significantly smaller than my other T-shirts."
"I would therefore like to exchange it."
I search briefly in my backpack.
I find the receipt immediately.
I place the T-shirt and the receipt on the counter.
"That is no problem at all," the assistant says.
She takes the receipt and looks at it.
